---
description: Keep commits and PR text free of tool attribution wording
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git commits and PRs: no tool attribution lines

- Do not include `Made with Cursor`, `Made-with: Cursor`, `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, or similar vendor/tool attribution lines in commit messages or PR descriptions.
- Do not include misspelled variants such as `Cusrsur` or similar wording.
- Keep commit messages focused on repository changes only.
- If a commit message must mention a tool name for a functional reason, do it only when the user explicitly asks.
